    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This is not an issue with 'mini.clue', but with how 'lazy.nvim' is used here to call configure 'mini.clues'. In the case of standalone plugin, executing `:=MiniClue` right after first step shows that `require('mini.clue').setup()` is called without supplied `opts`. While with 'mini.nvim' it does.\r\n\r\nI this is because 'lazy.nvim' does [special detection of 'mini.nvim'](https://github.com/folke/lazy.nvim/commit/dab6cd50806d6a6b0e8267f628d5fd6b112b151c) which might for some reason not work here.\r\n\r\nUsing `config` key instead of `opts` key for standalone plugin solves this.",
